java stamped call_construct="method" on every call with a receiver token,
so Files.readAllBytes(p) and System.getenv(k) read as receiver calls. The
unknown_receiver_scope caveat counts method edges as its denominator ("N of
M method call site(s)"), so every static call inflated M and the untyped
share read low. Go's twin was INV-tanom.

_java_call_construct stamps "function" when the receiver is a written FQ
type path, or a bare identifier that is a single-type import or a java.lang
class and is not a scoped variable or type parameter; otherwise "method".
Every such edge has a named module slot, so it is matched through the
module filter, never the no-context gate.

